{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1465548-howebrew-heroes","id":1465548,"title":"Howebrew Heroes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-10-27T12:20:46-07:00","id":1465548,"title":"Howebrew Heroes","content":"Sooooo here's the story: in one of my games, a Beast player messed up and caused a situation where tons of Heroes came after him at once, forcing me to come up with multiple Heroes at a time where I still wasn't that good at making them a real threat. With the help of a couple of friends, we designed some powerful Heroes for the opportunity, including several ones based on mythological Heroes. This is the result, and since the one time I showed one on a server people seemed to like them, I figured I could share them here.<br /> <br /> Here is my first attempt, a modernized version of our favourite Spartan King Leonidas. Enjoy.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>LEONIDAS</u><br /> Backstory: </b>Everyone knows by now about Leonidas 1rst of Sparta, the Spartan King who, during the Greco-Persan Wars. According to the Legend, he hold the line between the Persan Empire and Athens, with nothing but 300 men. Though they eventually fell thanks to a traitor, he and his men died heroically, allowing Athens to get the time that would later lead to the Greek victory. His body was later transferred to Sparta, and honored there.<br /> At least, that's the story people know.<br /> It's not clearly known what caused Leonidas to Awaken as a Hero back there. Some theorize that one of the Persan warriors was a Beast, and Leonidas slayed him in battle. Other says an entire squad of Persan Soldiers were actually a Brood, and he took them all down. Regardless of the truth, the fact is that, somehow, Leonidas Awakened on the battlefield - and one of the Gifts he acquires from his actions allowed him to recover from death, soon after the end of the celebration.<br /> Despite his miraculous recovery, Leonidas decided to not return to his throne; instead, he asked the few witness to cover his resurrection, left the power to his successors, and departed from Sparta. He no longer was a king; now he answered to a higher calling. He had discovered during his battle that monsters were real, and like the heroes of the old, it was his duty to hunt them.<br /> Nowadays, Leonidas still walks among the living, having prolongated his life further through the spectacular number of Beasts he slayed and gone through several fake identities; his most recent one is that of a rich and influent businessman, which he uses to travel around the world. Still nostalgic of his past, he founded a Cult, the Sons of Sparta, out of his followers, who help him hunt and preserve the traditions of his city.<br /> <br /> <b>Storytelling Hints:</b> One of the eldest Heroes, Leonidas dates back from fairly early (comparatively) in the History of Heroes, back in a time where they had not quite degenerated into the narcissistic psychopaths they are today. As a result, he is slightly more stable than the average Hero; though he considers it his duty to hunt Beasts, and has no scrupples murdering them, he also is concerned with protecting humanity from them and will do efforts to follow his Life as well. He should not be mistaken for a saint, though: being from Ancient Greece, his moral spectrum is exactly the one you'd expect from someone born in that time. Back then, it made him a brave and glorious king, but by today's standards, he's a cult leader training people to be professional killers and leading them at night or on battlefields to hunt Beasts.<br /> One particularly dangerous aspect of Leonidas is that, unlike many modern Heroes, he genuinely does care about his followers, albeit in some twisted way; he still won't hesitate to send them die against Beasts, which they usually are happy to do for him thanks to his indoctrination. But he sees each of them as a genuine brave warrior rather than a stepping stone to reach the Beasts, and whenever they die, he will mourn them and make sure they are buried with honor. This means the death of his followers tend to infuriate him, and make him all the more dangerous toward Begotten.<br /> <br /> <b>Legend :</b> Defender<br /> <b>Life :</b> Ruler<br /> <b>Attributes :</b> Intelligence 3, Wits 4, Resolve 5, Strength 3 (7 against Beasts), Dex 2, Stamina 4, Presence 4, Manipulation 2, Composure 5<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Athletics 3 (Lancer), Brawl 3, Expression 3 (Motivational Speech), Intimidation 2 (Stare), Occult 4 (Beasts), Persuasion 3, Subterfuge 1, Survival 2, Weaponry 7 (Spear)<br /> <b>Health:</b> 9<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 10<br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 6<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 9 (13 against Beasts<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 7 (6 if wielding Spear)<br /> <b>Defense: </b>7 (8 if opponent has a weapon shorter than a spear)<br /> <b>Armor:</b> 3/5 (5/5 against Beasts)<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Professional Training 5 (Warrior), Contacts 2 (Army, Finances), Ressources 4, Mystery Cult Initiation 5 (Sons of Sparta)*, Defensive Combat (Weaponry), Indomitable, Spear and Bayonet 3, Inspiring, Language (Ancient Greek, English)<br /> <b>Gifts: </b>Champion's Endurance, Chosen Blade, Vainquisher's Strength 2, Real World, Spartan's Last Breath*<br /> <b>Equipment:</b> Spear, Full Riot Gear, Helmet<br /> <b>Notes:</b><br /> * Leonidas' Asset Skills are Athletics, Weaponry and Intimidation;<br /> * His Chosen Blade is his Spear, which has the following stats (modified stats included): Damage 3, Initiative -1, Required Strength 2, Size 4; requires 2 hands, grants +1 Defense bonus against opponents with shorter weapons. His helmet also was modified to included sound filters, which protect him against sonic attacks such as Siren's Treacherous Song.<br /> * Leonidas rarely goes fighting Beasts without his Followers; unless caught by surprise, he typically is with at least a dozen of them, usually as heavily armed as him, with Full Riot Gear and Spears. He is a master strategist, and knows how to lead them effectively.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u><b>*New Gift: Spartan's Last Breath</b></u><br /> All Heroes are rather spectacularly hard to kill, but Leonidas takes it to a whole new level. This Gift was what saved his Life millenia ago, and helps him still run around on Earth. Not only is he capable of healing wounds at an accelerating rate, but even when on the door of death, he call upon his last strength and will to get up.<br /> The Hero may spend Willpower reflexively, up to 5 per turn, to heal as many lethal or bashing damages, or 3 WP to heal 1 Aggravated damage. In addition, once per session, if his Health is filled with Aggravated damage, he may immediately refresh his entire Health bar. Doing so, however, is exhausting and causes him to lose all his remaining Willpower at the end fo the scene.<br /> <br /> <b><u>*New Mystery Cult: The Sons of Sparta</u></b><br /> Founded by Leonidas to preserve the Spartan ideal, these hardened warriors are trained to fight against Beasts and other opponents with Spears and their will.<br /> * 1rst dot: The character has been trained into the basics of the Cult's fighting style; he gains a free specialty in Spears on the Weaponry skill.<br /> * 2nd dot: The character has learnt to use his Spear to Defend himself. He gets the Defensive Combat merit for Weaponry for free, regardless of if he meets the prerequisites or not.<br /> * 3rd dot: The character has forged his will to face monsters and not blink. He gets the Indomitable merit for free, regardless of if he meets the prerequisites.<br /> * 4rth dot: The character has refined his skills with the spear. He gets 3 free dots in the Spear and Bayonet merit, regardless of if he meets the prerequisites.<br /> * 5th dot: the character has been trained to use his spear in formation with the others. members with this level may do a teamwork action with their attack pools; if successful, they form a wall of spear to protect an area, inflicting their successes on anyone trying to go past them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11745,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","user":"Darinas","date":". 11-02-2021, 04:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T18:06:32-07:00","id":1465726,"title":"","content":"That's a pretty unique Hero Darinas! The Mystery Cult he founded seems pretty nice, though it doesn't list what the 5th dot does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27083-truemrmultiverse","name":"TrueMrMultiverse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27083_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T18:12:17-07:00","id":1465728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TrueMrMultiverse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1465548-howebrew-heroes?p=1465726#post1465726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a pretty unique Hero Darinas! The Mystery Cult he founded seems pretty nice, though it doesn't list what the 5th dot does.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, sadly I couldn't figure out what to add for the 5th dot yet. If you got suggestions, I'm open to it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T18:18:22-07:00","id":1465731,"title":"","content":"Hmmm. Maybe a sorta pseudo-Tactic like a where the Sons of Sparta make a human wall of spears perhaps?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27083-truemrmultiverse","name":"TrueMrMultiverse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27083_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T18:24:24-07:00","id":1465734,"title":"","content":"That could work, actually... I shall read the new Tactic rules and see what I can come up with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-07T07:52:12-07:00","id":1507688,"title":"","content":"Adding another homebrew Hero to my suggestions! This time someone from Orient, from a legend that inspired a certain Disney classic (and its significantly less classic Remake....):<br /> <br /> <b><u>HUA MULAN</u></b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Background:</b> In China, they tell the tale of Hua Mulan, a woman who once disguised herself as a man to join the army in her father's place to save his life. Though she helped bring victory to her country, by the time she came back home, her father had still died. When the Emperor then tried to take her as his consort, she committed suicide, and thus her legend remained.<br /> The truth, however, was slightly more complicated in the Chronicles of Darkness. Unbeknowst to many, one of the warlords she fought during the war was none other than a Beast, a Tyrant who fed by crushing conquered nations, and had been on the verge of Incarnation. Mulan was the one who took him down - and on the process, she Awakened as a Hero. One of the first Gift she gained from this was the ability to mask her identity and disappear in crowd; using this, she was able to fake her deaht and disappear, evading her fate. Since then, Hua Mulan has survived to this day, tracking down Beasts all over the globe and slaying them.<br /> <br /> <b>Storyteller Hints:</b> Part of what made her so enduring compared to most heroes is her pragmatism: not much of a glory hound like many younger Heroes, she prefers keeping a low profile, striking fast and efficiently before disappearing once again for a while. She has gone through many identities, and keeps moving whenever she feels she has done enough. Despite her best efforts, however, every now and then Beasts tell tales of a young asian man following them, only for someone to stab them while hearing a female voice whisper in their ear...<br /> <br /> <b>Legend :</b> Honorable</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Life :</b> Dutiful</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Attributes :</b> Intelligence 2, Wits 3, Resolve 3, Strength 3 (5 vs Beasts), Dexterity 4 (6 vs Beasts), Stamina 2, Presence 2, Manipulation 4, Composure 2</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Skills :</b> Academics 1 (Chinese Culture), Athletics 3, Brawl 3, Craft 2, Empathy 2, Occult 1, Persuasion 2, Stealth 2, Subterfuge 3 (Disguise), Weaponry 5 (Sword)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Health : </b>7</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Willpower :</b> 5</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Integrity :</b> 6</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Size :</b> 5</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Speed :</b> 14 (31 vs Beasts)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Initiative:</b> 5 (4 if using Weapon, 9 if sacrifice Weapon damage, ignore Initiative vs Beasts)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Defense:</b> 6 (8 with Sword, 9 with Sword and vs Beasts)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Armure :</b> 1/3 (3/3 vs Beasts)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Merits:</b> Language (Chinese, English, pick), Fleet of Foot 3, Striking Looks 2 (Beautiful), Quick Draw (Sword), Defensive Combat (Weaponry), Fighting Finesse (Sword), Light Weapons 3</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Gifts :</b> Chosen Blade, Champion\u2019s Endurance, Vainquisher Strength, Warrior\u2019s Speed 2, Be a Man !</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Equipment :</b> Chinese Sword, Kevlar Vest</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Note :</b><br /> * Mulan\u2019s Chosen Blade is a Chinese Sword, which has the following traits (modified stats included ) : Damage 3, Initiative -1, Strength 1, Size 3. Despite its Damage rating, it counts as a light weapon for the purpose of the Light Weapon merit - the increased damage is specifically due to the Chosen Blade bonus.<br /> * Mulan is most effective in stealth and hit-and-run tactics, using disguises to get close to beasts, then strike as hard as she can with her sword. If that doesn't kill them, she usually retreats using Warrior's Speed to come back later.<br /> <br /> <br /> * </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b><u>New Gifts : Be A Man !</u></b><br /> An unique Gift developped by Mulan during the time she spent in the Chinese Army, this represents her remarkable talent passing herself for a man and hiding her identity as a common soldier. Expanded on when she became a Hero, this has allowed her to disappear and become a deadly Beast slayer, hard to track by her opponent.<br /> A Hero with this Gift benefits from a +3 bonus on all rolls to disguise her identity, Blend in, or sneak attack. This can fool even supernatural senses (though a Clash of Will is necessary) and increases to +5 if she disguises in a gender opposite to hers. Moreover, she can carry weapon on her person and always successfully hide them. Even if she's carrying a sword or a similarly large weapon, people will magically not notice.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11745,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","user":"Darinas","date":". 04-08-2023, 09:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}